{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69","type":"heading","text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Interaction","type":"heading","text":"Interaction"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"to